<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Cadle Price</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/2011">2011</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as George Price of Belize</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Price led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-united-party">People's United Party</a>, founded in 1950 after the currency devaluation of 1949, and was the dominant figure of nationalism in British Honduras. He headed the government from 1961, became premier at self-government in 1964 and led the country, renamed Belize in 1973, to independence in 1981 as its first prime minister. He resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>'s claim to the territory and is honoured as the father of the nation.</p></div>
